ttps://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T14:09:42-07:00","id":238519,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Autumn House of Horrors</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> In this game, players take up positions within a building that has a minimum of five rooms +1 per player. Each player is given a token that gathers glamour created by fear, which they must harvest from mortals sent into the building (called the &quot;victims&quot;). The Autumn court is generally in charge of acquiring the victims, and is responsible for their safety if things get out of hand. Meanwhile, each of the players is restricted to a given room or area of the building (determined prior to starting the game). The player who gains the most points is the victor. Additional points may be earned through &quot;boasts&quot;; the player specifying who he intends to scare, how, when, and/or where. However, failure to achieve these boasts by the end of the game makes the player lose points equal to half the boast's worth. The referee (aka the Oathkeeper) is in charge of rules and regulations, as well as divvying up the points at the end of the game. To encourage longer running games, the Autumn Court will usually offer special prizes for those who gain exceedingly high scores, or complete particular boasts. The game ends when all the victims have vacated the building, or are rendered unconscious. Should the victims manage to somehow best the players, either by combat, deception, or remaining on the premises till sunrise the next day, the Autumn Court is obligated to reward them.<br /> <br /> <b>Da Rules</b><br /> <br /> 1. Players may not venture away from their designated territory. First offense is a warning. Second offense equals disqualification.<br /> <br /> 2. Players may not harm each other, nor the victims unless in self-defense.<br /> <br /> 3. Players may not block exits or entrances to other areas of the building, but may influence mortals to approach/avoid them.<br /> <br /> 4. Additional tokens are prohibited, as are lethal weapoons and/or toxins.<br /> <br /> 5. When deciding territories, players are disallowed from situating themselves in hallways, corridors, or the main entrances of the building.<br /> <br /> 6. A minimum of 3 victims is required to begin play.<br /> <br /> 7. All victims must be mortal. Encorcelled victims are allowed, but otherwise supernatural entities must be cleared by the Oathkeeper before play.<br /> <br /> 8. Boasts must be proclaimed prior to the start of play. The Oathkeeper determines the value of completing such boasts.<br /> <br /> 9. All contract, seeming, and kith abilities are permitted so long as they are not used to purposefully disfigure and/or kill.<br /> <br /> 10. Under no circumstances are players allowed to attack, antagonize, or bribe the Oathkeeper. In equal respect, the Oathkeeper is forbidden from taking such things, and must disqualify all players involved in said-actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"